    LLM: 'Game: Vint. Logic: See rules.objective and rules.gameplay.',
    Player: "Vint ('Screw') is a Russian partnership trick-taking game that influenced Contract Bridge's development. 4 players in 2 teams. 52-card deck. 13 each. Bidding (1-7 tricks over 6) with suit/NT denominations. NO dummy — all play own hands. Both sides score below-the-line for tricks won. First to 500 wins.",
    objective: 'Score points by winning tricks and making contracts; first partnership to reach 500 points below the line wins the game.',
    gameplay: 'Bidding: 1-7 (tricks over 6). Denominations: ♠<♣<♦<♥<NT. 3 consecutive passes end auction. Declarer plays against defenders. NO dummy. Follow suit. Both sides score below-the-line for tricks. Honors, slams, undertricks scored above-the-line.',
